sponse with Reactive RestResponse. It increased the score to 100 but it is using wrong message handler. Tried both ByteArray and InputStream as entity - same result\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nServerInputStreamMessageBodyHandler should be used write to response\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nUsing ServerStringMessageBodyHandler\r\n\r\n### How to Reproduce?\r\n\r\nUsing Kotlin\r\n\r\nDependencies:\r\n```\r\n    implementation \"io.quarkus:quarkus-resteasy-reactive\"\r\n    implementation \"io.quarkus:quarkus-resteasy-reactive-jackson\"\r\n    implementation \"com.fasterxml.jackson.module:jackson-module-kotlin\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\n@GET\r\n@Path(\"/{lectureId}/stream\")\r\n@Produces(MediaType.APPLICATION_OCTET_STREAM)\r\nfun getLectureStreamById(\r\n    @RestHeader(\"Range\") rangeParam: String?,\r\n    @RestPath lectureId: LectureId\r\n): Uni<RestResponse<InputStream>> {\r\n    return lectureAudioService.getAudioFile(lectureId).map { lectureStream ->\r\n            downloadResponse(ByteArrayInputStream(lectureStream.data), filename = \"$lectureId.mp3\").build()\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n\r\nfun downloadResponse(\r\n    data: InputStream,\r\n    filename: String,\r\n): ResponseBuilder<InputStream> {\r\n    return ResponseBuilder.ok(data)\r\n        .header(\"Content-Disposition\", \"attachment;filename=$filename\")\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Output of `uname -a` or `ver`\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Output of `java -version`\r\n\r\n17\r\n\r\n### GraalVM version (if different from Java)\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Quarkus version or git rev\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Build tool (ie. output of `mvnw --version` or `gradlew --version`)\r\n\r\n7.3\r\n\r\n### Additional information\r\n\r\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"stuartwdouglas","id":328571,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODU3MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/328571?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartwdouglas"